mainmenu "RadiANT heart-rate transmitter"

config HR_TX_ONE_WAY
	bool "Transmit only: never listen after a transmit"
	help
	  Open the channel as MASTER_TX_ONLY (0x50) instead of a bidirectional
	  MASTER (0x10). A bidirectional master opens a short receive window
	  after every transmit in case the receiver answers; a transmit-only
	  master never does, which saves that radio time on every message.

	  The cost: nothing the receiver sends can arrive (no page requests, no
	  acknowledged messages), and the ANT+ heart-rate profile says a strap
	  shall be a bidirectional master (Rev 2.5, sec 5.2.1, MD_0004).
	  Receivers still decode it. See the README's "Low power" section.

config HR_TX_RELEASE_HFXO
	bool "Release the HFXO between transmits where the radio backend can"
	imply RADIANT_NRF_LOW_POWER
	help
	  Turns on CONFIG_RADIANT_NRF_LOW_POWER (power plan Track B) wherever
	  its dependencies hold - the nRF54L15 and nRF52840 direct backends
	  with the LF crystal - and leaves it off without a Kconfig error
	  elsewhere (an LF clock synthesised from the HFXO, as the Pro Micro
	  clones without a 32 kHz crystal need, or an RC LF clock; the TI
	  boards), so lowpower.conf stays one fragment for every board.
	  build_all.ps1 asserts which rows end up with it.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
